 Indo-Gangetic Plain. It borders the Tibet Autonomous Region of China to the north, and India to the south, east, and west, while it is narrowly separated from Bangladesh by the Siliguri Corridor, and from Bhutan by the Indian state of Sikkim. Nepal has a diverse geography, including fertile plains, subalpine forested hills, and eight of the world's ten highest mountains, including Mount Everest, the highest point above mean sea level on Earth. Kathmandu is the nation's capital and its largest city. Nepal is a multi-ethnic, multi-lingual, multi-religious, and multi-cultural sovereign state, with Nepali as the official language.","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nepal","source":"Wikipedia","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","iso2":"NP"}],"arc":{"reports":25,"first_seen":"2026-10-10T22:58:29Z","first_title":"Climate Solutions Company Treasure Carbon Brings Climate Finance to Nepal for Long-Term Climate Action","first_url":"https://news.google.?oc=5","first_publisher":"GlobeNewswire","earlier":[{"id":"e_6b7e9bc03d12","title":"In first-ever climate crisis amends, Nepal to get $21.6 million","date":"2026-10-25T01:15:00Z","url":"https://news.google.?oc=5","publisher":"The Times of India","verification":"single_source_report"},{"id":"e_aca06973b293","title":"UN Climate Fund Provisionally Sets Aside $21.6 Million for Nepal After Bhote Koshi Flood Disaster","date":"2026-10-25T01:20:03Z","url":"https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMioAFBVV95cUxPeEc2T1RxUW5tbXB3NVJmUklyYV8wdGJnZFlRdEZiYnlFS2lsYUxKZldYUUtRVTdRRWI5WWNrLUNUamJCTHZJaUM1QTc2eGlKcnNDZE4ySFpDR0JmVDV5MUlkd2FrcXVuc3hZMnBYNWtIM1VrLUFxTW9DbUZNSkR6eHY5aFFJUUE3aEp4RmpfQWxtZGZYVXRYUHhyQUpKQVBH?oc=5","publisher":"www.nationpathindia.com","verification":"single_source_report"},{"id":"e_67c924e5182a","title":"Nepal to receive $21.6 million from UN climate loss and damage fund after deadly August floods","date":"2026-10-25T09:40:53Z","url":"https://news.google.?oc=5","publisher":"Moneycontrol.com","verification":"single_source_repo